.page trash 1 move files to the Netherworld

# SYNOPSIS
*trash* [*-fq*] _FILE_...

# DESCRIPTION
`trash` is `rm` with a second chance. Each _FILE_ is moved into `/Netherworld`, the directory where Yuyuko keeps what the living have let go of. If a file of that name is already there the newcomer is called `NAME.1`, `NAME.2` and so on. For each file one line says where it went.

Nothing in the Netherworld is deleted automatically. To get a file back, move it out again with mv(1); to forget it for good, remove it with `rm`.

# OPTIONS
@ *-q*, *-f*
    Quiet: say nothing, ignore files that do not exist.

The options `-r` and `-v` are accepted and ignored.

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if a file could not be moved.

# EXAMPLES
    trash draft.txt
    ls /Netherworld
    mv /Netherworld/draft.txt .

# SEE ALSO
rm(1), mv(1), gensokyo(7)
